Provisioning a Private MySQL RDS Instance
Step 1: Open the RDS Console
Log in to the AWS Management Console.

Search for and select RDS from the services menu.

In the left sidebar, click Databases, then click Create database.

Step 2: Set Creation Method and Engine Configuration
Under Choose a database creation method, select Standard create (Full configuration).

Under Engine options, select MySQL.

Select engine version 8.4.x from the version dropdown.

Under Templates, select Free tier.

Step 3: Set Instance Settings and Instance Type
In DB instance identifier, type datacenter-rds.

Configure the master username and password for database administration.

Under Instance configuration, set the DB instance class to db.t3.micro.

Step 4: Configure Storage Autoscaling
Under Storage, ensure Enable storage autoscaling is checked.

Set Maximum storage threshold to 50 GB.

Step 5: Configure Private Network Settings
Under Connectivity, choose your desired VPC and Subnet group.

Set Publicly accessible to No (to ensure it remains a private instance).

Attach the necessary VPC security group.

Keep all remaining settings at their default values.

Step 6: Create and Verify Availability
Click Create database at the bottom of the page.

Monitor the database list until the status for datacenter-rds updates from Creating to Available.
